  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 2D Chamfer with no picks generates again on a box stock under a tilted frame.\nThe check of #2887 no longer reads a wall that leans in the operation frame as a modelled chamfer.\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride.rs`: the new functions `leans` and `centroid`, the constant `LEAN_SLACK`, and one call in `partly_bevelled`.\n- `docs/decisions/2936-chamfer-leaning-wall.md`: the decision record.\n\nNo fixture changes. `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs` is not touched.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe fixture of #1700 is a 70 x 70 x 20 box stock with no part. The operation frame is tilted 10 degrees.\nIn that frame the top section (Z10) and the corner section (Z9) are the same rectangle. The top section is moved 0.176327 mm (`1 mm * tan(10 deg)`) in Y.\n`partly_bevelled` (#2887, PR #2894) compares each segment of the top loop with the wall loop.\nIt read the segments that touch the moved corners as bevelled. It read the middle segments of the X sides as sharp.\nIt then refused the loop with \"carries a modelled chamfer on only part of its length\".\nNo edge of the box carries a chamfer. The refusal was wrong for this model.\n\nThe loops of the fixture (from a debug print, not committed):\n\n- top: X -35..35, Y -33.776662..37.303201\n- corner: X -35..35, Y -33.952989..37.126874\n\n## The fix\n\n`leans(top, wall)` is true when the top loop is the wall loop moved whole by one plan vector.\nThe vector is the difference of the two area centroids. A collinear vertex does not change an area centroid.\nEach segment of each ring (two ends and the middle) must then be on the other ring within `LEAN_SLACK` (1e-4 mm).\nWhen `leans` is true, `partly_bevelled` returns `None`. `ride_loops` then rides the wall at the corner depth, as it did before #2887.\n\nA loop that carries a bevel on part of its length is not a moved copy of its wall. Its bevelled side moves in and its sharp sides stay.\nThus the refusal of #2887 holds for each case that it was written for.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_wall_leaning_in_the_frame_is_not_a_modelled_chamfer` (motion lib, new). It uses the loops of the fixture.\n- `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_moved_outline_with_one_side_bevelled_still_refuses` (motion lib, new). It guards the other direction.\n- `framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number` (app, `stock_source_holes`, not changed). This is the test of the issue.\n\nRed before the fix, on `upstream/main` afbf1590e:\n\n- The app test fails with the text of the issue (`... carries a modelled chamfer on only part of its length - it is sharp near X-35.000 Y-16.176 ...`).\n- The new unit pin fails with the same text.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- The call `leans(top, wall)` disabled: the new unit pin is red, and the app test is red with the text of the issue. Restored: the two are green.\n- `leans` replaced by `true`: `a_loop_bevelled_on_one_side_refuses_by_name`, `a_loop_bevelled_on_one_side_refuses_with_an_extra_vertex_too` and `a_moved_outline_with_one_side_bevelled_still_refuses` are red. Restored: green.\n\nThe old file was not copied back whole, because the new tests are in the same file. The disabled call gives the old behaviour.\n\nGate on the final source:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 4 steps, 0 failed (motion lib, `chamfer_modelled_edge`, `chamfer_partly_bevelled`).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test stock_source_holes`: 9 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test chamfer_partly_bevelled --test chamfer_modelled_edge`: 2 and 7 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nThe quick gate did not select `stock_source_holes`. Its gate map does not name `motion::machining2d::chamfer_ride`. I ran the suite by hand.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes and the release tier.\n- A tilted frame on a part with curved walls. The unit pin uses a rectangle only.\n- A part with a draft wall on some sides only, in an upright frame. Its two sections are the same as those of a modelled chamfer on those sides. The check of #2887 still refuses it and asks for picks. This PR does not change that.\n- macOS and Windows.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride.rs` or the `stock_source_holes` files.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer with no picks on a stock or part whose walls lean in a tilted operation frame generates again; it was refused as \"a modelled chamfer on only part of its length\".\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2936\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
